    <Image src={feb_15_56} alt="Humpback whale breaching off Cabo San Lucas" class="w-full h-48 lg:h-[300px] object-cover rounded-2xl mb-4 lg:mb-0 lg:w-1/2 lg:flex-shrink-0" width={800} height={500} />
    <div>
      <p class="text-base text-slate-500 leading-relaxed mb-3">Whales are mammals that breathe air and nurse their young. Humpbacks are known for their spectacular breaching and complex songs that can travel for miles underwater. Most whales in Cabo migrate from the cold waters of Alaska and Canada — they travel thousands of miles to the warm lagoons of Baja to mate and give birth.</p>
      <p class="text-base text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">The most common sightings here are humpback and gray whales. Occasionally, you may also spot blue whales, orcas, or whale sharks in the surrounding waters.</p>
      <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-light-grey rounded-xl p-3 text-center border border-border-light"><p class="text-navy font-bold text-lg">Dec–Apr</p><p class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 uppercase font-bold tracking-wider mt-1">Season</p></div>
